            "status": "succeeded",
            "output": "Review: Because `/` binds tighter than `-`, this computes `(sum(xs) / len(xs)) - 1`, which is the true mean minus 1; drop the `- 1` to fix it. It also raises ZeroDivisionError on an empty list.\n\nCAROL SAYS: Corrected version:\n\n    def mean(xs): return sum(xs) / len(xs)\n\nThe bug: `/` binds tighter than `-`, so the original computes `(sum(xs) / len(xs)) - 1`, which is the true mean minus 1. The arithmetic mean is just the sum divided by the count, so the `- 1` should go.\n\n(If `len(xs) - 1` was meant, as in a sample-variance denominator, that would be `sum(xs) / (len(xs) - 1)`. That isn't a mean, though, and it divides by zero for a single element.)\n\nOptional variant that handles an empty list instead of raising ZeroDivisionError:\n\n    def mean(xs): return sum(xs) / len(xs) if xs else float('nan')"
